Custom CSS:

/* Custom Styles for the Invoice */
.custom-invoice-wrapper {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
}

.custom-invoice-section {
    padding: 15px;
    border: 1px solid #ddd;
    border-radius: 5px;
    background-color: #f9f9f9;
}

.custom-invoice-title {
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #444;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
}

.custom-table th {
    background-color: #e8e8e8;
    color: #333;
    font-weight: bold;
    text-align: left;
}

.custom-table td {
    font-size: 16px;
    color: #666;
    padding: 8px;
}

.custom-table tr {
    border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;
}

.custom-table tr:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
}

.custom-invoice-section h4 {
    margin-top: 0;
    font-size: 18px;
    color: #333;
}

.custom-table td {
    vertical-align: middle;
}

@media (max-width: 768px) {
    .custom-invoice-wrapper {
        margin-bottom: 20px;
    }

    .custom-invoice-section {
        padding: 10px;
    }

    .custom-table td {
        font-size: 14px;
    }
}

Explanation:

1. General Styling:

The wrapper and sections are styled to create space between the various blocks, while the background color and border-radius add a modern touch.

The table headers are given a light grey background to differentiate them from the data cells.



2. Responsive Design:

The custom styles include media queries to ensure the invoice layout adapts well on smaller screens like mobile devices (below 768px).



3. Typography:

Larger font sizes and bold text are applied to the headings (h4 tags) to emphasize the section titles.

Table data has a slightly smaller font size to keep the content readable and clean.



4. Color Scheme:

Light gray backgrounds and borders provide subtle contrast and a soft look that doesn't overpower the text.




